From 5c0eb76bb3481f0989ad8659bf3c29f3cf5c7539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:29:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows: Wind Waker HD's caster culling and lava glow in
 its lit rooms (aurora_set_sun_caster_cull)

HD draws its shadow map's casters with their materials' cull mode (an HD capture of
Dragon Roost Cavern's room 0: 225 of its 240 map draws cull back faces, the
rest none), with its bias (80, 3) for the faces that do cast. RecompCore drew
every caster's both sides, so in a closed room the ceiling, seen from the room
light above, shaded the whole floor.

aurora_set_sun_caster_cull(on): the scenery's casters take their draw's own cull
mode (DrawData::sunCasterCull, front face clockwise as the scene's pipelines);
characters keep their own (none, or DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_CHARACTER_CULL).
DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_CASTER_CULL=1 or 0 overrides the host for tests. The host
turns it on in HD's lit rooms only; outdoors keeps both sides until it is
checked there.

Wind Waker HD's lava glow in its lava and fire rooms (GanonB, Cave01, MiniKaz,
Ganon's Tower's lava parts). HD's lava materials (PS 4345 in Cemu) add albedo
x lava K x 4 x the vertex red squared to the light, outside the shade, with
lava K the material's konst2 animation at the game frame (GanonB's capture:
0.453, 0.0415, 0.0005, its frame 23). A version 2 stage table has that curve
and each vertex's glow; a lit room draw in the GameCube's two-stage form (the
light, then x the texture) takes it from its vertices' colour 1 after the last
stage, and their share of the lit light goes through the sea mask's pass into
the normals' alpha, which the sun pass leaves unshaded. Cave01 goes from 0.47
to 0.97 of HD's brightness and from HD's red (0.77 red share) to its hue
(0.50, HD 0.49); GanonB from 0.60 to 0.86.
